NAME
    wmd - window manager daemon (Path C phase 5)

SYNOPSIS
    wmd [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Take over the framebuffer and run a compositor for SECONDS
    (default 30, then release).  Paints a desktop background, a
    top status bar, and four demo windows: a clock, an RGB
    gradient, an "About" panel, and a color-bars test card.

    Mouse interaction:
      hover         (no-op; cursor follows mouse)
      L click       raise the window under the cursor; if click
                    landed in the title bar, begin dragging
      L drag        move the dragged window with the cursor
      L release     stop dragging

    Cursor color encodes state:
      white         normal
      yellow        L pressed on desktop background
      red           L pressed in a window title bar (dragging)

    Top status bar shows "wmd - AdventOS Path C session 111".

    Compositor model is back-to-front blit at ~60 fps with libgfx
    double-buffering, so the present is atomic (no tearing).

LIMITATIONS
    No client protocol yet — all four windows are painted by wmd
    itself from its own pixel state.  Session 112 adds an IPC
    surface for real clients.

    The mouse driver only works if wmd is the FB owner.  Run
    `gfx` or `mouse` after wmd exits, not concurrently.

SEE ALSO
    mouse(1), gfx(1)
